<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Libya</h1><p class="st-meta">1951 CE – 1969 CE · capital Tripoli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent Libya under King Idris, a poor federal monarchy transformed by oil discoveries and overthrown by Gaddafi in 1969.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under a UN resolution, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> became independent on 24 December 1951 as a federal kingdom uniting <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Fezzan</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-of-libya">Idris al-Senussi</a>, ruler of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-cyrenaica">Emirate of Cyrenaica</a>, as King Idris I.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>At independence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> was among the poorest countries in the world, depending on foreign aid and rent from British and American bases such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wheelus-air-base">Wheelus Air Base</a>. The discovery of oil in 1959 and exports from 1961 brought sudden wealth. In 1963 the federation was abolished in favour of a unitary state. The king ruled conservatively, relying on Cyrenaican tribes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 1 September 1969, while Idris was abroad, army officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi">Muammar Gaddafi</a> seized power and declared a republic. Idris died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1983, and his flag was revived by the rebels of 2011.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-libya.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Libya" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Various The SVG code is valid. This vector image was created with a text editor. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Libya.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1951 CE – 1969 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tripoli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Idris I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United Kingdom of Libya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=kingdom-of-libya" aria-label="Kingdom of Libya on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5018 983 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Libya lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5338 1239L5380 1442M5338 1239L5338 1239M5338 1239L5516 1265"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5380 1442h0M5338 1239h0M5516 1265h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5338 1239h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tripoli. <a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=kingdom-of-libya">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
